Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-28-2000||05:02 PM||||Im in the process of changing my forward exhaust manifold (oodles of fun...)when I noticed that the head shield seems to be acting as the gasket. Is this correct? Its an 87 Gt. The heat shield is sandwiched between the manifold and head, then raps around. Dosnt appear to be a gasket. What gives? TIA, Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-28-2000||05:54 PM||||According to the local Pontiac garage, Fieros came from the factory with<B>out</B> exhaust manifold gaskets.  I guess they relied on perfect mating surfaces.||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||06-28-2000||07:46 PM||||Strange..........should I put one on (forward manifold)..if so, where? Like I said, the heat shield is sandwiched between the manifold and head........what to do?||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||06-28-2000||11:00 PM||||ive got an aftermarket turbo system on mine and used Felpro gaskets on both banks to be safe. sorry I dont have the part #||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||06-28-2000||11:22 PM||||I have in front of me, a GM service procedure, P/N 10154788 for Fiero/1987-88.  Has instructions for installing the recall package.<P>On sheet 2 of 10, it says (among other things):<P>"[Step] q.  Stack manifold deflector, gasket and manifold over new bolts and install (position on head using top bolts) using torque values described in Illustration A."<P>Then you go look at Illustration A (on sheet 4), and it shows a nice exploded view of how it all goes together.  It shows an oil deflector (I always called it a "heat shield") goes directly against the head, followed by a gasket, and then the manifold goes on, followed by a(nother) heat shield.<P>The (2nd) heat shield is held on by three little "tin nuts", I believe, that go onto the upper three exhaust manifold studs.<P>Not trying to argue, tell you what to do or anything   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  Just relaying what GM's instruction sheet says.  Hope this helps, and doesn't just add to the confusion   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 06-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||06-29-2000||09:31 AM||||Maybe one of the recalls included adding a gasket?  I'm just going by what the dealership told me since I'm mechanically challenged.||||reg||1
